---
title = "Raise Hex rate limits"
meta_title = "How to raise Hex rate limits"
subtitle = "with the Gleam command line"
description = "A read-only Hex API key can be used to raise API limits when resolving dependencies"
tags = ["gleam"]
---

Gleam uses the [Hex](https://hex.pm/), the package manager for the Erlang
ecosystem. Hex has rate limits for each IP address, and these can be hit when
performing multiple Hex-using actions within a short period of time, e.g.
updating the dependencies of multiple Gleam projects. A read-only API key can
be used to raise this limit. 

Create a new key via [the Hex dashboard](https://hex.pm/dashboard/keys), giving
it API read permissions.

Set this API key in the `HEXPM_READ_API_KEY` variable in the command line
session you are running Gleam from:

```shell
# Linux, MacOS, BSD, etc
export HEXPM_READ_API_KEY=01234567890123456789
```
```shell
# Windows PowerShell
$env:HEXPM_READ_API_KEY = "01234567890123456789"
```

Gleam will read this environment variable and use the key if present.
